# SABOTAGE: the gen-app post-step's transient rebar3 recovery is dropped — a dependency
# whose BUILD TOOL crashed (escript/rebar3 dying, not a compile error in the generated
# code) now aborts `compile_and_dump!/2` on the first attempt, exactly as it did on
# 2026-11-04 when the root gate died at the post-app probe while sibling gates loaded the
# box and the identical step then passed standalone.
#
# The plausible reasoning this encodes: "a failed dependency build is a failure; retrying
# it could mask a real one." The recovery is deliberately narrow — the error text must be
# Mix's `Could not compile dependency :<name>` line, the retry is bounded to ONE attempt,
# and a retry that fails too is re-raised with the retry's output. Without it, a transient
# build-tool crash kills a gate that would pass on an immediate re-run.
#
# POSITIVE CONTROL, deliberately untouched: the "genuine compiler error" test stays GREEN.
# The sabotage only removes the transient path, so a patch that flipped every test in the
# block would not be a targeted twin — and a retry that swallowed a real CompileError would
# still be caught by that control.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/gen_app_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a crashed rebar3 dependency build is cleaned and retried ONCE
# MUST_FAIL: a retry that fails too is raised
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/app.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/app.ex
index ab858611..7884907f 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/app.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/app.ex
@@ -609,7 +609,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Gen.App do
         :ok
 
       {out, code} ->
-        retry_transient_dep_compile(s, args, env, runner, out, code)
+        raise_mix_failure!(s, args, code, out, nil)
     end
   end
 
